bottomparticipants

actor Admin
boundary "Genre Management UI" as UI
boundary Router
control GenreController
control ValidationPipe
control GenreService
entity ":GenreModel" as GenreModel
database MongoDB

Admin -> UI: 1. Click "Add Genre" + submit form
activate Admin
activate UI

UI -> UI: 2. Validate required fields (name, description)
activate UI
space
deactivate UI

opt Missing name or description
    UI --> Admin: 2.1. Show error message
end
    
UI -> Router: 3. POST /genre
activate Router

loop Token invalid / Role invalid
    Router --> UI: 3.1. 401 Unauthorized
    UI --> Admin: 3.2. Show error message
end
    
Router -> GenreController: 4. create(dto)
activate GenreController

GenreController -> ValidationPipe: 5. Validate CreateGenreDto
activate ValidationPipe

opt Validation failed
    ValidationPipe --> GenreController: 5.1. Throw 400 error
    GenreController --> Router: 5.2. HTTP 400 response
    Router --> UI: 5.3. Validation error
    UI --> Admin: 5.4. Show error message
end

ValidationPipe --> GenreController: 6. DTO valid
deactivate ValidationPipe

GenreController -> GenreService: 7. createGenre(dto)
activate GenreService

GenreService -> GenreModel: 8. create(genre)
activate GenreModel

GenreModel -> MongoDB: 9. insert document
activate MongoDB
MongoDB --> GenreModel: 10. return result
deactivate MongoDB
GenreModel --> GenreService: 11. return result
deactivate GenreModel

opt Duplicate name
    GenreService --> GenreController: 11.1. Throw BadRequest
    GenreController --> Router: 11.2. HTTP 400 response
    Router --> UI: 11.3. Duplicate error
    UI --> Admin: 11.4. Show error message
end


GenreService --> GenreController: 12. Created genre
deactivate GenreService
GenreController --> Router: 13. HTTP 201 response
deactivate GenreController
Router --> UI: 14. Return created genre
deactivate Router
UI --> Admin: 15. Create genre success
deactivate UI
deactivate Admin

@enduml